[00:00] [scene:footage]
VISUAL: Sample footage from the Antigravity A1 drone.
AUDIO: 'This video is sponsored by Anti-Gravity. [music] &gt;&gt; [music]'

[00:24] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: Creator placing the Antigravity A1 drone on the ground.
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; Honestly, I\'ve never been a drone guy.'

[00:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I\'ve avoided flying drones for the majority of my career because they\'re risky, they\'re rather complicated to learn, and they require permits. But the anti-gravity A1 might just change that for me because it\'s a completely different way of flying. When you fly'

[00:53] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: Close-up of the Antigravity A1 drone controller, showing the record button and thumbwheel.
AUDIO: 'the A1, you get the feeling of being inside the drone, like a virtual reality game. It actually made me feel like I was up in the sky. Anti-gravity also lets you do difficult looking shots easily because you can add all the camera movements in post. So, it\'s great'

[01:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'for people who don\'t have much flying experience, but they still want to be able to get those FPV style movements. So, in this video, I\'ll walk you through the basic setup, how to control the drone for basic flight, doing FPV style camera moves by reframing in post,'

[01:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'filming human subjects for flyaway shots, low light filming, and trying out the sky path feature with my friend\'s dad, who has never flown a drone before. All right, so let\'s get started. You\'ve got your drone, your goggles, and'

[01:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'your controller. And I\'m going to talk about how you set up each of these, and then we\'re going to take them out and actually use them. First, you\'re going to take out your drone batteries. You can charge three of them at once, [music] and put one of them in the drone like this. The A1 has two lenses, one on'

[01:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'top and one on bottom. It also has other sensor cameras for obstacle avoidance, etc. And it has this cute little landing gear. So, you power on the drone like this. Then, you power your controller.'

[01:58] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: Creator wearing the Antigravity A1 goggles, holding the controller and drone.
AUDIO: 'Then, you get out your goggles and extend [music] the antenna. Then, you plug in the cable for the goggles battery. Turn on the goggles by powering on the battery unit. And then you might need to adjust the eye distance and the'

[02:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'diopter on the goggles to your own vision. [music] When everything\'s set up, this is how it\'s going to look. You\'re going to have the goggles on your head. You\'re going to have the lanyard around your neck with the battery. And then you\'re going to be holding on to the controller with the drone nearby ready to fly. One thing you might be'

[02:23] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: Creator outdoors, wearing goggles and holding the controller, preparing to fly the drone.
AUDIO: 'concerned about is that you are effectively blind when you\'re wearing these goggles. But if you double click on the left side, you\'ve got a camera built into your goggles, so you can see the real world around you. And then when you want to click out of that, you just'

[02:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'double click and you go back to the drone view. That\'s it. That\'s the basic setup. Let\'s get out there and start flying. Okay, I\'m about to take off. So, I\'m going to press the slider up twice and'

[02:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that starts the motors. And now I\'m going to push and hold the slider up and it will take off. All right. &gt;&gt; Okay. I\'m going to show you how to aim'

[03:00] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: Creator flying the Antigravity A1 drone outdoors.
AUDIO: 'the drone. Only the controller causes the drone to change its orientation. So for instance, if I shift the controller to the right, the drone looks that way. If I shift it this way, drone looks that way. And if I point it that way, points'

[03:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'forward. If I move my head, nothing happens. The head movement doesn\'t control [music] the direction that the drone faces. If you want to rotate the drone in place, you can turn the thumb'

[03:25] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: View from the drone goggles, showing flight telemetry and the landscape.
AUDIO: 'wheel on the controller and that will cause the drone itself to rotate left and right. So, that\'s different than turning your head cuz turning your head doesn\'t actually do anything [music]'

[03:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'physically. It just changes the direction the 360 camera is looking. If you want to actually change where the drone\'s facing, you use the hand wheel. When the drone\'s in the air, these goggles become your monitor. And here\'s the view that you\'ll see as it flies.'

[03:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'That cursor in the center is the target area that the drone is flying to. So, you can fly accurately without having to learn a joystick control just by aiming your trigger. As long as I keep that cursor in between the trees, [music]'

[04:03] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Split screen showing the drone goggles view and the creator wearing them.
AUDIO: 'then it will fly between them. Flying the A1 really does feel like you\'re up there flying, which unfortunately doesn\'t completely translate to a YouTube video. It\'s something you have to experience in real life. So, it\'s fun to use this thing'

[04:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'even if you\'re not making a video necessarily. [music] Even if you just want to use it as sort of a a real life video game, you can just look around. It\'s like having VR goggles on. You can effortlessly do FPV style shots'

[04:31] [scene:footage]
VISUAL: Cinematic drone footage over a city.
AUDIO: 'with the A1. All you have to do is a regular straightforward flight. [music] Then speed it up and add some roll or roll and tilt or whatever crazy angles you can come up'

[04:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'with. You can turn a standard flyover shot into something a lot crazier. This shot was intended to be just a straight rise up looking straight down,'

[04:58] [scene:footage]
VISUAL: Drone footage looking down into a narrow alley with a person.
AUDIO: 'but then I reinvented it in post by animating the roll parameter around the bell tower. For shots like these, I had to turn off the obstacle avoidance, but I still felt'

[05:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'pretty safe because I was flying slowly. You can always add the speed later. One of the things I was really hoping to use the A1 for is filming human subjects. Putting a person in the drone'

[05:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'shot gives it a sense of scale and it opens up a lot of storytelling opportunities. So, here\'s my first test shot with my friend Marco standing under the drone. He stood in place as I flew the drone straight up and then in post, I'

[05:37] [scene:footage]
VISUAL: Drone footage over rooftops.
AUDIO: 'refframed the shot to look straight down on him, but he was way too dark. So, I created a power window in Resolve to bring up his level. And then I tracked it to the shot. And here\'s the result. A shot starting'

[05:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'on Marco and then spiraling away as we rise upward. For the next shot, I was in a very narrow alley, so I turned off obstacle avoidance. And I flew facing away from'

[06:03] [scene:footage]
VISUAL: Drone footage flying through a narrow alley.
AUDIO: 'Marco for safety. I had an audience this time, so the pressure was on. So, here\'s my flight. I filmed looking forward to make sure I didn\'t hit anything on the way up. Then in post, I panned the'

[06:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'camera back to Marco. And now here\'s the final refframed version of the shot. Now, the results look really good, but I did notice one big limitation of the A1 while I was doing this shot, [music] the'

[06:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'stitch line. I wanted to start the shot at Marco\'s eye level, but this placed the gap between the lenses [music] over his face, which created some really obvious distortion. So, I had to move the drone to start over his head.'

[06:41] [scene:footage]
VISUAL: Low light drone footage of a landscape at dawn.
AUDIO: 'Hopefully, this can be improved with a redesign or with stitching algorithms in the future. [music] So, honestly, I wouldn\'t really recommend any 360 camera in extreme low light situations, but I still did want'

[06:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to try out the A1 in slightly more challenging lighting. So, I filmed these shots at dawn. At first, I tried to use a 1/50th shutter, which is the correct shutter speed for 24p shooting, but there was excessive vibration whenever'

[07:05] [scene:footage]
VISUAL: Low light drone footage of a town at dawn.
AUDIO: 'the drone was in the wind or whenever it changed directions. So, I bumped up the shutter to 180th, and that seemed to be good for slow flying in moderate wind. I found that a 1/60th shutter was the minimum to eliminate those vibrations'

[07:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and get a sharp image when I was flying faster. Here\'s some more late evening shots I did of the town of Chaldo Alto. Because I was filming really slowly and really carefully, I was able to keep that shutter very slow, around 1/50th to'

[07:31] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: Creator explaining the SkyPath feature while wearing the goggles.
AUDIO: '180th between the different shots. Remember, if you want the drone to look faster, you can always speed up the shot later. The next mission is to let my friend Marco\'s dad, who owns this property,'

[07:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'take a visual tour uh from the sky. But I don\'t want to make him actually fly the drone cuz that would require some instruction. So, what I\'m going to do is I\'m going to create a sky path, which is basically a preset path that the drone'

[07:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'will fly automatically. So, it\'s kind of like giving him a roller coaster ride. He just puts on the goggles and then I hit play and then it will fly along the path. So let\'s go into the menu and let\'s create the sky path. So I go'

[08:10] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Split screen showing the SkyPath recording UI in the goggles and the creator.
AUDIO: 'over here to sky path and then I create a route. So let\'s set one point here. Then I will fly out and set another point. Then let\'s'

[08:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'change directions. Maybe go out over the valley a little bit. Okay, we\'re setting another point. See that blue line getting longer every time I set a point? Let\'s save it. Now it\'s saved. Next, we put the goggles on Raphael and he'

[08:37] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: Marco's dad wearing the Antigravity A1 goggles.
AUDIO: 'watched the drone fly the path while riding on the back of a dragon. &gt;&gt; What does it look like? &gt;&gt; Incredible. [music] &gt;&gt; Each point on the path became a passing jewel.'

[08:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; How long have you lived here? &gt;&gt; Oh, 50 years ago I started to live here. &gt;&gt; Have you seen your property like this before? Have you? &gt;&gt; No, never. &gt;&gt; Oh, wow. &gt;&gt; Then Raphael said he wanted to fly it, so Marco gave him a quick lesson.'

[09:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; Are you letting him fly [music] now? Yeah, a little bit. &gt;&gt; Okay. &gt;&gt; So, now Rafael was in control. [music] &gt;&gt; Nice. Wow. &gt;&gt; Is it hard to fly? &gt;&gt; No. No. It\'s really intuitive. It\'s'

[09:14] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: Marco's dad wearing the Antigravity A1 goggles, looking around.
AUDIO: 'nice. &gt;&gt; He enjoys [music] it. He flies to the moon. [laughter] &gt;&gt; Do you think you can land the drone? &gt;&gt; Uh, yes. One moment, please. I enjoying'

[09:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that. &gt;&gt; Okay. No, you can fly until the battery goes dead. I don\'t care. A few minutes later, he was able to land the drone all by himself. &gt;&gt; You\'re fantastic. [laughter] And I hope you forget it here. Oh,'

[09:40] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: Creator demonstrating the Antigravity A1 drone flying.
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; you hope I leave it here. Okay. [laughter] &gt;&gt; So, after using the A1 for a few weeks, I found it to be a great way to get complex drone shots without requiring advanced flying skills. It\'s also safer because you can keep spatial awareness'

[09:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'by looking around and seeing everything around the drone. There are some quirks like learning to set up the goggles and use the controller, and it does take some new skills to properly reframe the footage. But if you\'re willing to learn a new way of doing things, it\'s an'

[10:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'amazing way to fly. Okay, so thanks so much for watching. If you want to learn more about the anti-gravity A1 or if you want to visit Marco\'s family at their winery, check the links in the description of the video and I will see you next'
